From 5fee9bd9800212c3e13af195d71d589512da514b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bench <bench@local>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 07:55:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 75/76] perf(sumcheck): materialize the partially evaluated
 tables after two rounds

The round-0 book-keeping table holds every prover polynomial at half the trace size next to the full
polynomials. For native Ultra/Mega flavors (HyperNova's instance sumcheck) and for the joint MegaZK +
translator sumcheck, the second round now reads the full polynomials folded at u_0 on access
(FoldedPolynomialView) and the tables are first built after it, at a quarter of the trace size, straight
from the full polynomials (fold_stride4_backed). Every table entry and round univariate is computed
exactly as before.
